/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak
/corpus/data/
/corpus/cache/
# bench/results/raw/ was ignored wholesale. That silently un-published the
# measured evidence for three ACCEPTED ADRs, so a reader who cloned the
# repository could not check any of them:
#
#   adr2-git-baseline-django.json, adr2-source-sweep.json -> ADR-2 (chunking)
#   adr3-store-bench.json                                 -> ADR-3, ADR-4
#   adr3-fsync-bench.json                                 -> ADR-4
#
# The names carry the ADR the measurement was PRODUCED for; the arrows say who
# cites it. adr3-fsync-bench.json is the F_FULLFSYNC-versus-fsync(2) benchmark
# run during ADR-3's storage work and cited by ADR-4 for the daemon's group
# commit — and it is what establishes that fsync(2) is not crash-safe on macOS,
# which ADR-18 in turn rests on.
#
# The four files total 24 KB and are now committed; genuinely large raw output
# can be ignored by name when it appears.
/harness/.venv/
/prototypes/*/target
.DS_Store
*.profraw
/tmp/
/.lattice/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
harness/lib/iofault/*.dylib
harness/lib/iofault/*.so
harness/lib/iofault/*.o
